  "bound_assumptions": [
    "Doppler scenarios boost both delayed-photon energy and its total source energy. The actual maximum resolved final bulk factor is recorded;1.10 is an additional finite envelope, not a mathematically absolute thermal-particle speed limit. Saved grey-prompt energy is already a model escape-energy account and its20MeV scenario is specified in the laboratory frame.",
    "Piecewise log-linear NIST coefficient interpolation, with no smaller energy-absorption coefficient below1keV than the stated minimum; low-energy photons ultimately absorbed rather than upgraded back into hard photons.",
    "Local charged-secondary energy deposition and photon regeneration at the collision location. Nonlocal electron and positron transport is not solved.",
    "No photon energy upscatter by a hot material. Receiver at~1000K, apart from transient heating, versus keV/MeV photons.",
    "Closed shell returns inner-directed photons to another receiver patch; no ports/gaps and no credit for heat received in cold components.",
    "Energy-weighted exponential transport bound uses the minimum mu_en over all down-scattered photon energies, not incident mu_en.",
    "Removing20/50kg/m2 from the bound illustrates sensitivity to an assumed boundary layer; it is not a rigorous replacement for coupled electron-photon transport."
